{%- liquid
  assign logo_text = section.settings.logo_text | default: shop.name
  assign menu = section.settings.menu
  assign tagline = section.settings.logo_tagline
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The bar is three groups — menu, wordmark, tools — and the layout setting
  decides the order they sit in. They are captured first and printed in that
  order below, rather than reordered with CSS, so the source order always
  matches what is on screen and tab order follows the eye.

  The defaults on the two spacing values guard against a stored header whose
  settings predate them. An empty value would emit "--hdr-gap-left: px", and an
  invalid custom property makes the whole declaration compute to its initial
  value — the spacing would collapse and the control would appear to do nothing.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    The layout class is always written, the centred one included, so every
    layout's rules can be written the same way round instead of one of them
    having to be expressed as "not the others".
  endcomment
  assign layout = section.settings.layout | default: 'centre'
  assign hdr_class = 'hdr hdr--logo-' | append: layout
-%}

{%- capture group_menu -%}
  <div class="hside hside--left">
    <button
      type="button"
      class="menu-toggle"
      data-drawer-open="NavDrawer"
      aria-label="{{ 'general.open_menu' | t }}"
      aria-controls="NavDrawer"
    >
      <span></span><span></span><span></span>
    </button>

    <nav class="hnav" aria-label="{{ 'general.menu' | t }}">
      <ul>
        {%- for link in menu.links -%}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ link.url }}" {% if link.active or link.child_active %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
              {{- link.title | escape -}}
              {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
                <span class="caret">{% render 'icon', name: 'caret' %}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </a>
            {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
              <div class="sub">
                {%- for child in link.links -%}
                  <a href="{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title | escape }}</a>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
{%- endcapture -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Image or wordmark is an explicit choice rather than "an image if one was
    uploaded". A merchant trying a logo out and then wanting the wordmark back
    should not have to delete the file to get there.

    The type overrides go through the same text-style snippet every other
    section uses, so the wordmark answers to the same three controls — font,
    size, colour — as every other piece of type in the theme. Size arrives as
    --ts, a multiplier, which scales the tagline with the mark rather than
    pinning either to a pixel value.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign use_image = false
    if section.settings.logo_type == 'image' and section.settings.logo != blank
      assign use_image = true
    endif
  -%}
  {%- capture logo_type_style -%}
    {% render 'text-style', s: section.settings, key: 'logo' %}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- capture logo_mark -%}
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="logo" style="--logo-width: {{ section.settings.logo_width }}px;{{ logo_type_style }}">
      {%- if use_image -%}
        <img
          src="{{ section.settings.logo | image_url: width: 400 }}"
          alt="{{ shop.name | escape }}"
          width="{{ section.settings.logo.width }}"
          height="{{ section.settings.logo.height }}"
        >
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="logo-mark">
          {{- logo_text | escape }}<b>{{ section.settings.logo_text_light | escape }}</b>
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The tagline sits under the mark for an image logo too — a merchant with
        a logotype but no strapline baked into it still wants the line.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if tagline != blank -%}
        <span class="logo-tag">{{ tagline | escape }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The wordmark is the page's h1 on the home page only; every other template
    has a heading of its own. Either way it gets the same real wrapper.

    It used to be an h1 with display:contents on the home page and no wrapper
    at all elsewhere, which meant the group in this slot was sometimes a box and
    sometimes not. A box that is not there cannot take a margin, so the spacing
    settings silently did nothing whenever the wordmark sat at an end of the bar.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture group_logo -%}
    {%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
      <h1 class="hlogo">{{ logo_mark }}</h1>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="hlogo">{{ logo_mark }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- capture group_tools -%}
  <div class="hside hside--right">
    {%- comment -%}
      The tools read as icons, so each carries its label in a visually hidden
      span rather than a title attribute — a title is not reliably announced
      and never reaches a keyboard-only user.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="htools">
      {%- if section.settings.show_account and shop.customer_accounts_enabled -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.account_url }}" class="hicon htool-account">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'account' %}
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'sections.header.account' | t }}</span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.show_search -%}
        <button type="button" class="hicon" data-search-open aria-controls="SearchPanel">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'search' %}
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'sections.header.search' | t }}</span>
        </button>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if settings.cart_type == 'drawer' -%}
        <button type="button" class="hicon hicon--bag" data-drawer-open="CartDrawer" aria-controls="CartDrawer">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'bag' %}
          {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
            <span class="bag-n" aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="visually-hidden">
            {{ 'sections.header.bag' | t }} — {{ 'sections.header.bag_count' | t: count: cart.item_count }}
          </span>
        </button>
      {%- else -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" class="hicon hicon--bag">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'bag' %}
          {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
            <span class="bag-n" aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="visually-hidden">
            {{ 'sections.header.bag' | t }} — {{ 'sections.header.bag_count' | t: count: cart.item_count }}
          </span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endcapture -%}


{%- comment -%}
  Only the colours actually chosen are written out. An empty colour setting
  renders as nothing, and `--hdr-ink-set: ;` is not the same as leaving the
  property alone: an empty token stream is a valid custom property value, so
  var() would take it instead of its fallback and every rule reading it would
  collapse. Emitting a property only when there is a colour to put in it leaves
  the stylesheet's fallbacks doing their job.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ink = ''

  if section.settings.ink != blank
    assign ink = ink | append: '--hdr-ink-set:' | append: section.settings.ink | append: ';'
  endif

  if section.settings.ink_hover != blank
    assign ink = ink | append: '--hdr-ink-hover:' | append: section.settings.ink_hover | append: ';'
  endif

  if section.settings.ink_current != blank
    assign ink = ink | append: '--hdr-ink-current:' | append: section.settings.ink_current | append: ';'
  endif

  if section.settings.ink_over != blank
    assign ink = ink | append: '--hdr-ink-over:' | append: section.settings.ink_over | append: ';'
  endif
-%}
<header
  class="{{ hdr_class }}"
  id="SiteHeader"
  data-stick="{{ section.settings.stick | default: 'hero' }}"
  style="--hdr-gap-left: {{ section.settings.gap_left | default: 90 }}px; --hdr-gap-right: {{ section.settings.gap_right | default: 90 }}px;{{ ink }}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The middle slot is the centred one. The wordmark takes it when it is
    centred; otherwise the menu does, and the icons take whichever side the
    wordmark left free.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- case layout -%}
    {%- when 'left' -%}
      {{ group_logo }}{{ group_menu }}{{ group_tools }}
    {%- when 'right' -%}
      {{ group_tools }}{{ group_menu }}{{ group_logo }}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ group_menu }}{{ group_logo }}{{ group_tools }}
  {%- endcase -%}
</header>

{%- comment -%} Mobile navigation {%- endcomment -%}
<nav class="nav-drawer" id="NavDrawer" aria-label="{{ 'general.menu' | t }}" aria-hidden="true">
  <header>
    <h2>{{ 'general.menu' | t }}</h2>
    <button type="button" data-drawer-close>{{ 'general.close' | t }}</button>
  </header>

  <ul>
    {%- for link in menu.links -%}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
        {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="sub">
            {%- for child in link.links -%}
              <a href="{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title | escape }}</a>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>

  {%- comment -%}
    On a phone the bar has no room for the menu and the tools at once, so the
    tools come in here and sit with the links as one list — search, account and
    bag as words rather than marks, since there is space to name them and a
    label is quicker to read than an icon.

    Opening search or the bag from in here needs no special handling: both
    triggers close whatever drawer is open before they act.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <ul class="nav-drawer-tools">
    {%- if section.settings.show_search -%}
      <li>
        <button type="button" data-search-open aria-controls="SearchPanel">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'search' %}
          {{ 'sections.header.search' | t }}
        </button>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.show_account and shop.customer_accounts_enabled -%}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ routes.account_url }}">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'account' %}
          {{ 'sections.header.account' | t }}
        </a>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}

    <li>
      {%- if settings.cart_type == 'drawer' -%}
        <button type="button" data-drawer-open="CartDrawer" aria-controls="CartDrawer">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'bag' %}
          {{ 'sections.header.bag' | t }}
          {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
            <span class="bag-n" aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="visually-hidden">
            {{ 'sections.header.bag_count' | t: count: cart.item_count }}
          </span>
        </button>
      {%- else -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'bag' %}
          {{ 'sections.header.bag' | t }}
          {%- if cart.item_count > 0 -%}
            <span class="bag-n" aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="visually-hidden">
            {{ 'sections.header.bag_count' | t: count: cart.item_count }}
          </span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </li>
  </ul>
</nav>

{%- if section.settings.show_search -%}
  <div class="search-panel" id="SearchPanel" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- if settings.predictive_search_enabled -%}<predictive-search>{%- endif -%}
      <form action="{{ routes.search_url }}" method="get" role="search">
        <label for="SearchInput" class="visually-hidden">{{ 'general.search.title' | t }}</label>
        <input
          type="search"
          id="SearchInput"
          name="q"
          value="{{ search.terms | escape }}"
          placeholder="{{ 'general.search.placeholder' | t }}"
          autocomplete="off"
          {% if settings.predictive_search_enabled %}
            role="combobox" aria-expanded="false" aria-autocomplete="list"
          {% endif %}
        >
        <button type="button" data-drawer-close aria-label="{{ 'general.search.close' | t }}">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'close' %}
        </button>
      </form>

      {%- if settings.predictive_search_enabled -%}
        <div class="predictive" data-predictive-results></div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.predictive_search_enabled -%}</predictive-search>{%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

<button type="button" class="scrim" id="Scrim" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></button>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Header",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-header",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "logo_type",
      "label": "Logo",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "text",
          "label": "Wordmark (text)"
        },
        {
          "value": "image",
          "label": "Image"
        }
      ],
      "default": "image",
      "info": "Image falls back to the wordmark when no file is set, so the header is never blank. That fallback is also why Image is the default — a store that already had a logo uploaded keeps showing it after an update rather than reverting to text."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "logo",
      "label": "Logo image"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "logo_width",
      "label": "Logo width",
      "info": "Applies to the image only.",
      "min": 60,
      "max": 260,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 110
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "logo_text",
      "label": "Wordmark",
      "info": "Defaults to your store name."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "logo_text_light",
      "label": "Wordmark tail",
      "info": "Joined to the wordmark above and set in the same weight. Leave it empty unless you are splitting the name across two fields."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "logo_tagline",
      "label": "Tagline",
      "info": "A short line under the wordmark, set small and letterspaced — 'Skin care', 'Est. 1998'. Two or three words at most; it is not a place for a sentence."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Wordmark type"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "logo_font",
      "label": "Font",
      "info": "The three fonts themselves are set in Theme settings, so the wordmark stays part of the same type system as the rest of the theme.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "default",
          "label": "Default"
        },
        {
          "value": "heading",
          "label": "Heading font"
        },
        {
          "value": "body",
          "label": "Body font"
        },
        {
          "value": "accent",
          "label": "Accent font"
        }
      ],
      "default": "default"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "logo_size",
      "label": "Size",
      "info": "Scales the wordmark and its tagline together, and stays responsive rather than pinning them to one pixel size.",
      "min": 50,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "logo_color",
      "label": "Colour",
      "info": "Leave empty to follow the colour scheme."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Bar colours"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Applies to the menu links, the search, account and bag icons, the menu button, and the wordmark. Leave any of them empty to follow the colour scheme, which is the safe choice: a colour set here is used everywhere, including where the bar sits on the page's own background. If you want light labels only while the bar floats over a hero picture, use the last setting in this group rather than this one. A colour set on the wordmark itself, above, wins over these."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "ink",
      "label": "Menu, icons and wordmark"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "ink_hover",
      "label": "On hover",
      "info": "Also colours the line that sweeps in under a link. Empty means hover keeps the colour above and only brightens."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "ink_current",
      "label": "Current page",
      "info": "The link for the page a visitor is already on. Empty follows the scheme's accent colour."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "ink_over",
      "label": "Over a hero picture",
      "info": "Used only while the bar is floating over a hero set to run under it, before the visitor scrolls. Empty means white, which is what carries over a photograph."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "Bar layout",
      "info": "Where the wordmark sits. The menu and the icons take the other two places around it.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "left",
          "label": "Logo left · menu centred · icons"
        },
        {
          "value": "centre",
          "label": "Menu · logo centred · icons"
        },
        {
          "value": "right",
          "label": "Icons · menu centred · logo right"
        }
      ],
      "default": "centre"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "stick",
      "label": "When the bar takes its background",
      "info": "While a hero is set to run up under the bar, the bar is clear and its text is light so the picture shows through. This decides when that ends. Waiting for the picture keeps it clear for as long as there is something behind it worth seeing; the other option turns it solid the moment the page moves.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "hero",
          "label": "Once the picture has passed"
        },
        {
          "value": "page",
          "label": "As soon as the page moves"
        }
      ],
      "default": "hero"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_left",
      "label": "Space on the left of centre",
      "info": "The air between the centred group — the wordmark, or the menu when the wordmark is at an end — and whatever sits to its left. In pixels, exactly as set. Narrow screens ease it back so nothing crowds.",
      "min": 20,
      "max": 750,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 90
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_right",
      "label": "Space on the right of centre",
      "info": "The same on the other side. The two can differ — the centred group stays on the centre of the bar either way, so uneven values give it uneven air rather than pushing it off centre. Wide settings leave the menu less room, so a long menu folds into the drawer sooner.",
      "min": 20,
      "max": 750,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 90
    },
    {
      "type": "link_list",
      "id": "menu",
      "label": "Menu",
      "default": "main-menu"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_search",
      "label": "Show search",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_account",
      "label": "Show account link",
      "default": true
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "groups": [
      "header"
    ]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
